## Generation Entry Points

The store exposes three generation entry points, all routing into `handleGenerateInternal(targetIndices?)`:

| Method | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `handleGenerate()` | Generate all pending (no filter) |
| `handleGenerateSingle(targetIndex)` | Generate a single config → `handleGenerateInternal([targetIndex])` |
| `handleGenerateFiltered(targetIndices)` | Generate a subset → `handleGenerateInternal(targetIndices)` |
| `handleRegenerateSingle(targetIndex)` | Generate one new variant for an already-generated card (see § Regeneration below) |
| `handleRegenerateConfig(targetIndex)` | Card "Regenerate" button. Text-to-audio card whose edits touch only per-variant inputs (prompt, duration…; `hasCardLevelGenerationChanges` false) → `regenerateVariantInPlace(i, selectedVariant)`: only the selected variant is replaced. Otherwise (variant count / speech lines edited, TTS) → regenerate ALL variants via `handleGenerateInternal([i], { force: true })`: same deterministic event ids (links survive); variants beyond `seed_copies` are dropped + pruned. "+" does not raise `seed_copies`, so routing per-variant edits to a full regenerate would collapse A + B into one new A. |

`handleGenerateInternal` (at soundscapeStore.ts:392) is the core orchestrator. It:
1. Skips already-generated config indices (tracks `alreadyGenerated` set from `soundscapeData`) — unless `force` targets them
2. Splits configs by type: ML generation (TangoFlux/AudioLDM2), ElevenLabs, TTS, upload, library, catalog
3. For ML: submits via `apiService.generateSounds()`, polls via `getSoundGenerationStatus()` (wraps the unified `GET /api/jobs/{job_id}`), streams `partial_sounds` into `generatedSounds` as each sound completes
4. `mapBackendSound()` remaps batch-relative IDs to config-absolute IDs to avoid collision
5. Merges results into `soundscapeData` and `generatedSounds`

## Level Calibration — One Anchor, Levels Applied at Playback

Every sound file the backend writes goes through `utils/loudness.py::calibrate_loudness`: TangoFlux,
AudioLDM2, Stable Audio 3, TTS, and `/api/calibrate-audio` (upload, sample, library, catalog,
ElevenLabs, FX-editor Save) plus SED extraction (`calibrate_audio_file`).

1. **Measure** ITU-R BS.1770 gated integrated loudness (K-weighting, 400 ms blocks, −70 LUFS
   absolute + −10 LU relative gates). The gates skip silence and quiet tails, so a sparse event is
   measured on its active part. One vectorized pass: no loop/segment search.
2. **Gain** to `TARGET_LOUDNESS_LUFS + (target_dbfs − DEFAULT_DBFS)` (boost capped at
   `LOUDNESS_MAX_GAIN_DB`; a file entirely below the absolute gate is left untouched).
3. **True-peak limiter** at `TRUE_PEAK_CEILING_DBTP`: only the overs are reduced. Never scale the
   whole file down to fit its peak (that made punchy sounds quieter than steady beds).

Denoising runs between a gain-only normalization (`limit=False`) and the final calibration.

**Files are calibrated to the global base anchor (`globalBaseDbfs`), never to a sound's own level.**
A card's `dbfs` / orchestrator SPL travels as the event's `volume_dbfs` and is applied at playback as
`volume_dbfs − globalBaseDbfs`. Baking it into the file too applies it twice. The clip plans keep
both: `dbfs` (returned as `volume_dbfs`) and `calibration_dbfs` (= `base_dbfs`, what the worker
calibrates to). Every `generateSounds` call passes `base_dbfs`; TTS items and SED extraction send
`globalBaseDbfs` as their calibration level.

**Background beds get a lower level band.** A bed plays continuously and everywhere without distance
falloff, so at the same dB value it sounds ~15 dB louder than an event. `BACKGROUND_BED_DBFS_*`
(`config/constants.py`) is the band (−50..−34, default −42). Both level-estimating prompts quote it via
`_bed_level_guidance()` (`llm_service.py`), and code clamps the result: orchestrator bed entries
(`_bed_spl`, which also fills a missing level) and sound-list sounds with raw `INTERVAL: 0` and no entity.

**Final bed level is derived from the scene (frontend, last step).** `applyBackgroundAutoLevels(cardIndices)`
(`soundscapeStore.ts`, maths in `lib/audio/utils/bed-auto-level.ts`, constants `BACKGROUND_AUTO_LEVEL`) runs
after a generation finalizes (inside the bake callback when the scene is orchestrated, directly otherwise) and
after a re-orchestration's bake. Per scene (`parentUsageOriginalIndex`): each non-muted event track's level
minus its distance loss to the selected receiver (1/r, fallback distance without a receiver), weighted by the
share of the timeline it plays (baked `soundTimestamps` + durations, else its interval loop), energy-summed;
each bed = that − `MARGIN_DB`, clamped to the bed band (positioned beds add back their own distance loss).
It overwrites the LLM's bed level (the backend clamp stays as a safety net), writes the card `dbfs` + events'
`volume_dbfs`, and skips a bed whose fader the user moved (`soundVolumes`). It is NOT run on later DAW edits.

The live master limiter (`AUDIO_CONTROL.LIMITER`, also the export's post-render ceiling) is a −1 dBFS
safety net for the summed mix, so per-sound levels stay linear dB offsets.
`orchestrator.getLimiterReductionDb()` / `OutputDiagnostics.limiterReductionDb` report it.

## Scene Realism Inputs (scenario pipeline)

- **Atmosphere** (`liveliness`: calm / normal / lively) is sent to the scenarist, foley and speech
  agents; `SCENE_LIVELINESS_LEVELS` (backend) / `SCENE_LIVELINESS_OPTIONS` (frontend) are one table.
- **Recurring foley** (`FoleySoundEvent.recurrence`) is expanded in code
  (`utils/recurrence.expand_recurrence`): `timestamps` and `copyCount` are derived, so the card's
  variant count follows the number of occurrences. `recurrence` is kept in `scenarioSource` so a
  re-orchestration rebuilds the trigger chain.
- **One-shots** (`FoleySoundEvent.oneShot`, foley rule 10): the LLM labels short discrete sounds
  (impacts, knocks, page turns). The label passes through orchestrate (`OrchestrateEntry.oneShot`)
  to the card's `one_shot`. ElevenLabs then gets no `duration_seconds` (auto length; a forced
  estimate only pads with silence); TangoFlux/SA3 clips get `trim_silence` per clip → `noise_trim`.
  The trim region (`utils/audio_processing.compute_noise_trim_region`, also behind "Trim silence")
  confirms onset gaps on the RMS envelope and cuts the trailing silence after the last sound
  (`TRIM_*` in `config/constants.py`). SA3 needs `librosa` in `compas-sa3` for it.
  Sustained LLM sounds send their duration to ElevenLabs; beds and manual prompts never do.
- **Crowd murmur bed**: `utils/crowdBed.withCrowdBed` appends a background foley entry (and its
  selection key) after foley + speech when more people are present than speak; it is generated like
  any other bed card.

## Backend — Hash-Based Deduplication

The clip plan builder (`routers/sounds.py::_build_clip_plan`) computes a parameter hash to determine the output filename:

```python
param_string = f"{prompt}_{duration}_{guidance_scale}_{steps}_{apply_denoising}_{audio_model}"
param_hash = hashlib.md5(param_string.encode()).hexdigest()[:PARAM_HASH_LENGTH]
filename = f"{short_prompt}_{param_hash}_copy{copy_idx}.wav"
```

If the file already exists, the GPU worker **skips** generation and returns the existing file URL.
This means identical parameters produce identical filenames — perfect for deduplication on re-submission,
but **prevents regeneration from producing a genuinely new file**.

### Regeneration Uniqueness Fix

For regeneration (user clicks "+" on a variant bar), the frontend adds `_regeneration_ts: Date.now()`
to the config dict. The clip plan builder checks for this field:

```python
# routers/sounds.py — _build_clip_plan()
regeneration_ts = cfg.get("_regeneration_ts", "")
if regeneration_ts:
    param_string += f"_{regeneration_ts}"
```

**The hash lives in a single place — `routers/sounds.py::_build_clip_plan`.** Keep the
`_regeneration_ts` field in sync with the frontend; omitting it causes silent deduplication on
regenerate.

## Variant System

Each sound config can produce multiple variants (controlled by `seed_copies` in the config).
Variants share the same `prompt_index` but have unique `copy_index` values (0, 1, 2, ...).

### Store fields

| Field | Store | Purpose |
|-------|-------|---------|
| `soundConfigs[]` | `soundscapeStore` | Configuration cards. Index = `prompt_index`. |
| `generatedSounds[]` | `soundscapeStore` | All sound events. `prompt_index` links back to config. `copy_index` differentiates variants. |
| `soundscapeData` | `soundscapeStore` | Same as `generatedSounds` but `null` when empty (used for save/restore). |
| `selectedVariants: Record<number, number>` | `audioControlsStore` | Which variant index is selected for each config. Defaults to 0. |
| `regeneratingIndices: number[]` | `soundscapeStore` | Config indices currently being regenerated (reactive state, shows spinner in UI). |

### Key functions

**`handleVariantChange(promptIdx, variantIdx)`** — `audioControlsStore.ts:240`:
Switches the active variant. Stops preview playback of old variant, updates `selectedVariants`.
Frontend components read `selectedVariants` to know which variant to display.

**`getVariantsForPrompt(index)`** — `SoundGenerationSection.tsx:257`:
Filters `generatedSounds` by `prompt_index` to return all variants for a card.

**`getSelectedVariantIdx(index)`** — `SoundGenerationSection.tsx:262`:
Returns `selectedVariants[index] ?? 0`.

### Regeneration (`handleRegenerateSingle`)

Located at `soundscapeStore.ts`. Called when user clicks "+" on the variant bar.

1. Prevents duplicate regeneration via `regeneratingIndices` check
2. Computes `maxCopyIndex` from existing variants to avoid ID collision
3. Auto-switches to predicted new variant: `handleVariantChange(targetIndex, currentVariantCount)`
4. Sends config with `seed_copies: 1` and `_regeneration_ts: Date.now()` for unique filename
5. Polls backend, maps results with incremented `copy_index` and `id: "generated_{targetIndex}_{newCopyIdx}"`
6. **Must include `geometry: sound.geometry || { vertices: [], faces: [] }`** in mapped events — otherwise `SoundSphereManager` crashes with "Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'vertices')"
7. Adds/removes `targetIndex` from `regeneratingIndices` for UI spinner display

### Delete Variant (`handleDeleteVariant`)

Located at `soundscapeStore.ts`. Called when user clicks "×" on a variant square.

1. Sorts variants by `copy_index`, validates index and minimum count (>1)
2. Removes target sound from `soundscapeData` / `generatedSounds`
3. Adjusts `selectedVariants` if the deleted variant was selected (shifts down by 1)
4. Audio file remains on disk — only the reference is removed from app state

## Variant Bar UX (SoundResultContent)

The variant bar (A / B / C squares) is shown **only for text-to-audio cards** (`showVariantSelector` prop).
Other card types (upload, library, catalog, TTS) have no variant bar.

| Element | Condition | Behavior |
|---------|-----------|----------|
| A, B, C… squares | Always | Click to switch variant. Active variant uses card-color background. |
| Spinner square | `isRegenerating` is true | Shows animated spinner. Clickable but plays no audio yet. |
| **+** button | `onAddVariant` provided & not regenerating | Triggers `handleRegenerateSingle`. Only on text-to-audio cards. |
| **×** delete button | `variants.length > 1` & `onDeleteVariant` provided | Appears on hover (group-hover), removes variant from store. |

When the pending variant is selected during regeneration, `SoundResultContent` renders a
"Regenerating..." placeholder instead of the WaveSurfer waveform.

## Card Lifecycle — Pre-Gen vs Post-Gen

`SoundGenerationSection.renderCard()` determines which content to show in the `Card`'s `beforeContent` vs `afterContent` slots:

| State | `beforeContent` | `afterContent` | Card styles |
|-------|----------------|----------------|-------------|
| **Pre-generation** | `SoundPreContent` (config UI) | `undefined` | Collapsed info shows "(pending)" |
| **Post-generation** | `undefined` | `SoundResultContent` (waveform + variant bar) | `hasResult=true`; settings section = `SoundPreContent settingsOnly` (TTA/TTS/library/catalog), "Regenerate" once edited |

The transition is gated by `isSoundGenerated(index)` which checks if any `generatedSounds` entry has a matching `prompt_index`.

## Event Mapper Comparison

When adding new event-mapping logic, ensure it matches the existing `mapBackendSound` pattern in
`handleGenerateInternal` (lines ~519-582). Key fields every mapped event must carry:

- `id` — unique per variant, format `generated_{promptIndex}_{copyIndex}`
- `prompt_index` — links back to `soundConfigs` array index
- `copy_index` — integer variant number
- `position` — `[x, y, z]` world position
- `geometry` — `{ vertices: [], faces: [] }` or the backend-provided geometry
- `entity_index` — optional, for entity-linked sounds
- `url` — static file URL or blob URL for the WAV file
- `duration` — seconds (float)
- `volume_db` — SPL level
- `interval_seconds` — loop interval
